{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03071",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.06,
      "end_seconds": 4.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. May I come in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.63,
      "end_seconds": 10.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "You're alright, take a seat. What can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.93,
      "end_seconds": 17.09,
      "duration_seconds": 6.16,
      "text": "Doctor, it's headaches most days. It's getting on my nerves now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.38,
      "end_seconds": 22.63,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "Since when exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.58,
      "end_seconds": 25.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "It's been two months now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.58,
      "end_seconds": 38.18,
      "duration_seconds": 10.6,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.09,
      "end_seconds": 48.51,
      "duration_seconds": 8.42,
      "text": "So, it settles a little with painkillers. Mostly severe. I didn't want to make a fuss, you know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.92,
      "end_seconds": 52.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Any other symptoms with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.11,
      "end_seconds": 60.07,
      "duration_seconds": 5.96,
      "text": "Light sensitivity goes along with it, uh, most of the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.98,
      "end_seconds": 63.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Have you been feeling sick?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 65.18,
      "end_seconds": 69.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "I mean, yeah. About four days, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.19,
      "end_seconds": 73.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "Any visual changes, fever, stiff neck or weakness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.52,
      "end_seconds": 77.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "No, none of those at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.21,
      "end_seconds": 81.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "Anything on the skin I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.66,
      "end_seconds": 83.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.12,
      "text": "Skin's normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.86,
      "end_seconds": 88.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Do you live by yourself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.96,
      "end_seconds": 94.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.29,
      "text": "No, I share a house with my brother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.3,
      "end_seconds": 98.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Do you work outside the home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.99,
      "end_seconds": 102.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.49,
      "end_seconds": 108.91,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "Do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.5,
      "end_seconds": 114.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "No, nothing as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 115.44,
      "end_seconds": 118.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.07,
      "end_seconds": 126.2,
      "duration_seconds": 7.13,
      "text": "I've, I've had migraines, yes. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.4,
      "end_seconds": 147.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "What do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 149.89,
      "end_seconds": 153.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Propranolol, 40 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.09,
      "end_seconds": 157.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "Time for your numbers, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.76,
      "end_seconds": 166.75,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "Sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.22,
      "end_seconds": 192.86,
      "duration_seconds": 7.64,
      "text": "Okay: blood pressure 127 over 77, pulse is 68 beats a minute, temperature is 36.5 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.65,
      "end_seconds": 195.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.69,
      "end_seconds": 200.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "I'll interpret them after the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.29,
      "end_seconds": 204.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "I'll examine you in a second, make yourself comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.04,
      "end_seconds": 207.27,
      "duration_seconds": 1.23,
      "text": "Does that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.75,
      "end_seconds": 225.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "Your neurological examination is normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 236.4,
      "end_seconds": 237.33,
      "duration_seconds": 0.93,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.03,
      "end_seconds": 243.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.21,
      "end_seconds": 258.45,
      "duration_seconds": 8.24,
      "text": "Let me tell you where I've got to. My working impression is medication-overuse headache on a background of migraine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 260.14,
      "end_seconds": 262.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "What are the odds it's serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.91,
      "end_seconds": 284.44,
      "duration_seconds": 19.53,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with medication-overuse headache on a background of migraine do well once it's treated properly. Let me repeat that back to make sure. You've had headaches most days for two months, severe, and no stiff neck or weakness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 286.27,
      "end_seconds": 289.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "Yes, um, you've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.61,
      "end_seconds": 294.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Let's book a headache diary to look into daily headache."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 299.42,
      "end_seconds": 300.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Does it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.65,
      "end_seconds": 333.9,
      "duration_seconds": 32.25,
      "text": "We'll begin with amitriptyline, 10 milligrams, at night, long term. That should help with headache prevention. Stop the daily painkillers gradually, the headaches may worsen for a couple of weeks first. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think. I'd like to see you again in six weeks. Let me check I've been clear. What will you do once you get home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 335.65,
      "end_seconds": 344.07,
      "duration_seconds": 8.42,
      "text": "So, I take the amitriptyline, 10 milligrams, at night and come back in six weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 345.35,
      "end_seconds": 350.74,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 352.3,
      "end_seconds": 355.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Thank you, uh, doctor, goodbye."
    }
  ]
}